Emacsvox News -- History Of User-Visible Changes

Maintained by Emacsvox Contributors.

* Emacsvox 2026.9.1 --- Current User-Visible Changes

This corrective release requires Emacs 31 or later and Omnivox 1.6.4 or newer.
The guided WSL2 installer pins the matching verified Omnivox 1.6.4 Windows x64
or ARM64 archive.

- The spoken ``Emacsvox is ready.'' checkpoint now waits for acknowledged
  initial engine inventory, routing policy, and logical voices, so normal first
  speech uses the restored engine preference.  A bounded capability-ready
  fallback retains an audible checkpoint if routing does not complete.

- Windows Omnivox staging now authenticates and prewarms the bounded eSpeak
  voice cache for its verified content-addressed data, avoiding repeated native
  voice discovery during later fresh Emacsvox launches.

- Opt-in Aural Presentation diagnostics now correlate native submission IDs
  with Omnivox dispatch IDs and record actual dispatch send, first observed
  mixer-source consumption, and terminal playback timing.  Omnivox's normal
  session log supplies the matching server admission, queue, synthesis, and
  playback-stage breakdown without a speech protocol change.  Use =C-e d D=
  to toggle the sensitive, full-text diagnostic log for the current session.

- The source-built Windows Omnivox runtime now uses the Omnivox 1.6.4 source
  and matching checksum-locked Piper companion.  It includes RuTTS 6.3.3 and
  its built-in male and female Russian voices; RuLex remains excluded.  Staging
  now finishes with live Flite and RuTTS voice discovery and WAV-synthesis
  checks against the Windows-local payload, and the WSL launcher forwards an
  explicit =OMNIVOX_RUTTS_HELPER= override.
